<!--
  THE LAUNCHER SYMBOL, BUILT TO THE MEASUREMENT RATHER THAN TO TASTE.

  MANTRA_MANIFEST/modules/app-icon.md: the launcher hands out a 108 canvas and shows the centre
  72. The symbol goes in a 42 box centred in that, which puts the drawn edge at 0.583 of the
  visible circle, inside the 0.55 to 0.60 band measured from icons drawn by people who measured.

  The glyph is the Material "timer" icon, path data unchanged from the official set. It is one
  shape plus its crown, which is the fewest shapes that say stopwatch.

  The arithmetic, so nobody has to rediscover it:
    the icon's ink in its own 24 viewBox runs x 3..21 and y 1..22, so 18 wide by 21 tall
    scale 2.0 makes that 36 by 42, and 42 is the box
    translate 30, 31 puts the centre of the ink on 54, 54
-->
